pplicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IDEMITSU KOSAN CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWAMURA HISAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA HIROAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HOSOKAWA, CHISHIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IDEMITSU KOSAN CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWAMURA, HISAYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HOSOKAWA CHISHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWAMURA HISAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA HIROAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HOSOKAWA, CHISHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWAMURA, HISAYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An organic electroluminescent device comprises an anode, a semiconductor layer, an organic luminescent medium, and a cathode.  Assuming that a first electrode is either an anode or cathode and a second electrode is the other, an organic luminescent medium is provided between the first electrode and a semiconductor layer with no single-crystal material, and the second electrode is connected electrically with an edge of the semiconductor layer.  Since the first and second electrodes do not face each other, various electrode materials can be used, and the luminescent area increases, thus providing a brighter organic electroluminescent device.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif organique électroluminescent comprenant une anode, une couche semi-conductrice, un milieu organique luminescent et une cathode. Sachant qu'une première électrode est soit une anode soit une cathode, et qu'une seconde électrode est le pendant anode ou cathode, on fournit un milieu organique luminescent entre la première électrode et une couche semiconductrice sans matériau à cristal unique, et la seconde électrode est reliée électriquement à un bord de la couche semiconductrice. Puisque les première et seconde électrodes ne se font pas face, on peut utiliser différents matériaux d'électrode, moyennant quoi la zone luminescente augmente et l'on obtient ainsi un dispositif organique luminescent plus clair.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>